---
import SiteLayout from '../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { getBuildMode } from '../../../lib/build-mode.js';

const mode = getBuildMode();
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Purpose-Driven Food Brands & Retailers | Terra Nexus"
  description="Terra Nexus helps food brands, manufacturers, retailers, and their partners connect purpose, product design, sourcing, evidence, claims, customer experience, and commercial performance."
  preview={mode === 'preview'}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">TRANSFORMED INTO FOOD &amp; FEED</p>
    <h1>Turn Better Products and Sourcing into Trusted Market Value</h1>
    <p class="hero-lead">Terra Nexus helps food brands, manufacturers, retailers, and their partners connect purpose, product design, sourcing, evidence, claims, customer experience, and commercial performance.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Discuss Your Product Opportunity</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/capabilities/">Explore Our Capabilities</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Definition and Scope</h2>
      <p>Purpose-driven food brands and retailers connect purpose, product, sourcing, evidence, pricing, channel execution, and claims — and ensure operations can deliver what the brand promises.</p>
      <h3>Topic Boundaries</h3>
      <ul class="topic-boundaries">
        <li>Other Areas of Expertise address upstream production systems and supply-chain operations</li>
        <li>This topic focuses on product, brand, and retail commercialization</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why This Topic Matters</h2>
      <blockquote class="market-thesis">Purpose creates commercial value when the product proposition, sourcing model, customer need, evidence, pricing, channel execution, and claims are designed together — and when operations can deliver what the brand promises.</blockquote>
      <p>A sustainability claim or purpose story that is not anchored in product reality, sourcing evidence, and operational delivery creates exposure rather than value. Customers, regulators, and civil society increasingly scrutinize the gap between what a brand says and what it can prove. The brands that capture durable value are those that design the proposition, the product, the sourcing, the evidence, the pricing, and the channel execution as one system — so that every claim is supported, every promise is delivered, and every margin is earned.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Primary Value-Chain Position</h2>
      <p><strong>Food &amp; Beverage; Retail &amp; Distribution.</strong> Relies on upstream Ingredient &amp; Feed Processing, Commodity Trading, Agricultural Production, and Inputs.</p>
      <p>This topic sits at the commercial end of the value chain, where product, brand, and customer meet. It depends on upstream sourcing, processing, and production systems to supply the evidence and attributes that make purpose credible — but its focus is how that credibility is translated into product strategy, category position, customer trust, and commercial performance.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Primary Audiences</h2>
      <div class="audience-grid">
        <article class="audience-card">
          <h3>Food &amp; Beverage Companies</h3>
          <p>Co-lead audience. Manufacturers and brand owners connect purpose to product design, sourcing, evidence, claims, pricing, and channel execution — and must ensure operations can deliver what the brand promises.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="audience-card">
          <h3>Food Retail &amp; Distribution</h3>
          <p>Co-lead audience. Retailers connect category strategy, supplier standards, customer-facing assurance, and claims to shelf placement, private-label differentiation, and customer trust.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="audience-card">
          <h3>Agricultural Producers &amp; Integrated Protein Companies</h3>
          <p>Alignment with downstream brand and retail requirements, producer economics, evidence and traceability, and commercial participation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="audience-card">
          <h3>Commodity Traders</h3>
          <p>Connecting origination, attributes, and evidence to brand and retail demand for responsible, differentiated, and low-impact products.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="audience-card">
          <h3>Ingredient &amp; Feed Processors</h3>
          <p>Sourcing, footprinting, traceability, low-emissions and differentiated ingredients, byproduct value, and claims support.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="audience-card">
          <h3>Enabling Tech &amp; Solution Providers</h3>
          <p>Market entry, product strategy, technical diligence, pilot design, partner selection, and integration into brand and retail workflows.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Decisions Clients Face</h2>
      <div class="decisions-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Brand, Category &amp; Portfolio Owners</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Which sustainability or purpose proposition solves a meaningful customer problem?</li>
            <li>How does the proposition connect to category strategy, brand architecture, and portfolio roles?</li>
            <li>What premium or margin can the market support, and who captures the value?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Product, Sourcing &amp; R&amp;D</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Which sourcing, product, packaging, formulation, or service changes are required?</li>
            <li>How to connect product design to sourcing evidence and supply-chain reality?</li>
            <li>What evidence, footprinting, certification, and assurance support the intended claim?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Marketing, Claims &amp; Regulatory</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>How should claims adapt by channel, geography, customer, and regulatory context?</li>
            <li>What assurance level and substantiation does each claim require?</li>
            <li>How to manage claims across markets with diverging rules?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Channel, Commercial &amp; Operations Teams</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Can operations consistently deliver what the brand promises?</li>
            <li>How does purpose translate into shelf placement, category access, and customer experience?</li>
            <li>What controls, evidence, and reporting sustain the proposition at scale?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Representative Value Pathways</h2>
      <p>The same underlying product and sourcing improvement may support different claims with different levels of rigor, cost, commercial reach, and value. The best pathway is not always the claim with the highest nominal price.</p>
      <div class="pathway-tags">
        <span class="pathway-tag">Branded-product differentiation and premium</span>
        <span class="pathway-tag">Retailer qualification and category access</span>
        <span class="pathway-tag">Certification and ecolabel claims</span>
        <span class="pathway-tag">Product environmental-footprint claims</span>
        <span class="pathway-tag">Customer loyalty and trust value</span>
        <span class="pathway-tag">Portfolio and brand-architecture value</span>
      </div>
      <p class="pathway-note">These are categories of potential value, not promises that every pathway is available, stackable, transferable, or commercially superior. Detailed pathway analysis remains client-specific.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How Terra Nexus Capabilities Apply</h2>
      <div class="capability-mapping">
        <article>
          <h3><a href="/capabilities/strategy-and-innovation/">Strategy &amp; Innovation</a></h3>
          <p>Market, growth, business-model, product, program, and partner strategy; opportunity assessment, segmentation, positioning, and commercialization; pilot design and build-buy-partner decisions.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3><a href="/capabilities/financial-investments-and-new-venture-development/">Financial Investments &amp; New Venture Development</a></h3>
          <p>Business cases, scenario analysis, value allocation, and initiative prioritization; investor, technology, project, program, and transaction diligence; capital, partnership, and portfolio decisions.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3><a href="/capabilities/sustainable-supply-chain-and-operations/">Sustainable Supply Chain &amp; Operations</a></h3>
          <p>Sourcing, supplier, producer, traceability, and chain-of-custody design; operating models, governance, systems, controls, and implementation; recurring program management.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3><a href="/capabilities/corporate-sustainability/">Corporate Sustainability</a></h3>
          <p>Impact measurement, inventory and target alignment, disclosure, and governance; product, value-chain, climate, nature, resilience, and claims integration; stakeholder communication.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3><a href="/capabilities/carbon-and-ecosystem-services/">Carbon &amp; Ecosystem Services</a></h3>
          <p>Market-mechanism and methodology assessment; environmental-program design, MRV, valuation, commercialization, and management; verification readiness, evidence, and claims translation.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How Terra Nexus Engages</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Advise</h3>
          <p>Terra Nexus evaluates opportunities, performs diligence, models economics, defines strategy, selects frameworks and partners, and designs programs, systems, controls, and commercial structures.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Manage</h3>
          <p>Terra Nexus embeds within client-owned programs to coordinate recurring evidence, data, calculations, ledgers, partners, exceptions, reporting, and verification readiness.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-dark">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <h2>Build Purpose into Products Customers Can Trust</h2>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Discuss Your Product Opportunity</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .topic-boundaries { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .topic-boundaries li { padding: var(--space-2) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .topic-boundaries li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .market-thesis { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: var(--text-lg); font-style: italic; color: var(--color-text); padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .audience-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) { .audience-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .audience-card { padding: var(--space-4); background: var(--color-bg); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
  .audience-card h3 { font-size: var(--text-base); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .audience-card p { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .decisions-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-6); grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) { .decisions-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .decisions-grid h3 { font-size: var(--text-base); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .decisions-grid ul { padding-left: var(--space-5); }
  .decisions-grid li { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .pathway-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2); margin: var(--space-4) 0; }
  .pathway-tag { font-size: var(--text-xs); padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); background: var(--color-bg); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .pathway-note { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .capability-mapping { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) { .capability-mapping { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .capability-mapping article { padding: var(--space-4); background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
  .capability-mapping h3 { font-size: var(--text-base); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .capability-mapping h3 a { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .capability-mapping p { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .text-center { text-align: center; }
  .text-center .hero-actions { justify-content: center; }
  .section-dark .btn-primary { background: #fff; color: #1a1f24; border-color: #fff; }
  .section-dark .btn-primary:hover { background: #e2e5e9; border-color: #e2e5e9; }
</style>
